WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.480
Before, you could see us renovating this old ruin.

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:04.400
The whole thing is not straight at all.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.720
No wall is 90 degree in here,
and they're just built very sketchy...

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:11.240
So, we built a wooden frame inside
that would carry the load of the roof.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:16.640
We've also built back the broken top,
and now the wood and the bricks are connected to each other.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:19.640
So, now, we actually have one
solid structure to continue with.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:24.440
Now that the ruin walls are connected again, 
we can finally cut our last hole right there.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:28.600
We didn't do this before, because we were a bit skeptical, 
if the wall would actually hold it...

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:32.520
And, we will use the bricks we get,
 to close the old entrance right there.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:37.287
So, in this video, we're going to make a cut,
patch back a wall, and build a window frame.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:39.280
And Martijn and Adrian are going to make it!

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:46.400
So, first step, we are going to cut the bricks,
to open a window.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.280
We are not really sure about this.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:53.240
So, we have these old concrete...

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:57.920
But, we are not sure,
 if it's going to really hold the full wall.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:01.760
So, we are going to add a metal lintel here for that.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:05.040
We also have Martijn, the expert from the Netherlands
to help us.

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:07.560
Hi! My name is Martijn!

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:12.240
I'm a maker and, I just had my birthday here, and I turned 33!

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:18.360
In my last job, I was an engineer for a company
 that makes cardboard houses.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:23.160
And now, I'm at Project Kamp to help
make a sketchy ruin less sketchy.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:26.920
Besides making things, I like to make music.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:32.960
And, I love dancing!

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:36.440
Someday, I would like to live
in a community with my girlfriend.

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:38.160
Let's see what the future brings!

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:40.640
First cut!

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:35.071
We have cut this size, because then,
 we can straight away put it in the door. 

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:38.160
It will fit exactly the same there.

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:39.280
So, let's work, let’s clean the tiles...

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:50.040
The wall was still stuck...

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:53.040
And, we had to do some more cutting...

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:34.629
So, we finished the first half of the hole for the window!

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:42.000
And, before I continue, I'm going to make sure that all
 of what's left here, is not going to fall on my head...

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:48.040
I'm going to put a metal support in this corner.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:20.440
All the cuts in the wall have been made, 
and now it's time to take out the last bit of wall.

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:57.400
The cut is ready!

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:58.760
We are still alive.

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:00.850
And, look at the view!

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:07.280
So, the next step, we place the metal lintel on top.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:09.840
We will introduce it in the wall,
while making some cuts.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:13.240
We fill the gap with cement
to make everything a bit more sturdy.

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:02.880
The next step is to put the steel lintel in position.

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:06.640
And, to get it up to the right height.

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:19.825
All right!

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:22.640
Now, we have the lintel in place.

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:27.880
We're going to put cement over here,
and in that corner to keep it in place.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:23.720
So, on both sides, we've now filled the space
between the lintel and the bricks.

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:26.800
It's already starting to dry a little bit.

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:30.680
And now, we're just going to be filling
 on the other side of the wall.

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:56.880
Before, you could see that we were filling in the space,
 between the brick and the metal lintel.

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:58.459
But, as you can see...

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:01.948
These bricks are all hollow.

00:08:03.035 --> 00:08:04.945
Probably not so strong...

00:08:04.945 --> 00:08:10.600
So, we're going to fill all the gaps,
 withsome cement to make it a bit more strong.

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:44.520
We've been cutting the hole before.

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:49.040
This used to be a door, and we were going to close it,
because we made a door on the side.

00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:52.200
We like to reuse stuff.

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:56.600
So, we decided to use the whole section,
and just put it in place.

00:08:57.040 --> 00:09:02.320
After this is in place,
we'll use new bricks to fill in the top.

00:10:06.333 --> 00:10:10.320
For the big hole we cut in the wall now, 
we are going to make a window frame.

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:14.800
We got gifted some really nice,
insulated glass panels by Ronald.

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:18.440
A Dutch guy that lives around here.

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:22.000
Thanks, Ronald, for that!

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:26.850
And, around those glass panels, 
we're going to make a wooden window frame.

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:30.760
We asked some local woodworkers
to give us a jump start.

00:10:30.760 --> 00:10:36.560
By making some really nice straight timber
for us, with a nice groove to put the glass.

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:39.560
So, we've got eight windows,

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:42.920
First, we're going to make an outside frame.

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:49.570
Then, in the middle, we're going to place another vertical one.

00:10:49.570 --> 00:10:55.791
And then, we have three horizontals,
 to end up with eight windows.

00:10:56.625 --> 00:10:59.265
So, here's the design for the window frame!

00:10:59.265 --> 00:11:05.480
The window frame itself is made up of 
an outside frame, and an inside frame.

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:09.600
The glass panels sit in a groove
that's cut into wooden beams.

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:13.040
And, they are held in place by a glazing bar.

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:15.360
Today, Emma is going to help me.

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:16.597
Let's start cutting!

00:11:17.836 --> 00:11:19.673
- That's me, baby!

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:17.440
Just finished the window frame!

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:19.760
It’s over there!

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:20.920
I'm pretty happy with it.

00:13:20.920 --> 00:13:22.720
It's nice and tight!

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:27.080
There's not so much steady machinery and flat surfaces...

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:30.080
So, I'm pretty happy how it turned out!

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:13.480
- It's like this, I think?

00:14:13.480 --> 00:14:16.280
So, we already put the window on.

00:14:16.280 --> 00:14:19.440
We tried to solve a couple of problems
we have in this ruin.

00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:22.920
One of them is, like, there's
not a single surface that is leveled.

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:24.653
Nothing is balanced.

00:14:24.653 --> 00:14:25.557
Nothing is square.

00:14:26.012 --> 00:14:30.315
As you can see here, like, this wall is a bit like this...

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:33.800
Then, this wall is not square with this one....

00:14:34.080 --> 00:14:42.160
So, we are going to make a frame now,
 to be able to level all our new surfaces a bit.

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:44.320
Including the window, and the window is already level.

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:50.240
We need to put it higher a bit on one side,
 than on the other one, in order to have it level.

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:54.280
And then, when the window is level,
also the water will flow in a better way.

00:14:54.320 --> 00:14:59.160
If we don't have the window level,
the water will be stuck in some places...

00:14:59.840 --> 00:15:06.360
So, the next step is to build the frame around, 
fix it and continue with the job!

00:15:39.760 --> 00:15:44.280
We have test-fitted the window frame 
in the hole, and it fits pretty well!

00:15:46.306 --> 00:15:52.760
I gave it some sanding, and I've cleaned up the edges of the frame
with a router, to make it all nice and smooth.

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:55.480
Now, it's time to paint it.

00:15:55.480 --> 00:16:01.720
We're going to use a clear coat varnish,
in order to keep the wood good for a longer time.

00:16:01.720 --> 00:16:03.800
And besides that, it's going to be painted.

00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:10.080
It's going to be under overhang of the roof, 
which will protect the window frame from rain and the sun.

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:13.800
Which is going to make it last for a longer time!

00:16:40.320 --> 00:16:47.240
Now that the window frame has been painted,
in a nice, clear varnish, you can still see the beautiful pinewood.

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:49.960
We are going to put the glass.

00:16:49.960 --> 00:16:53.240
The glass is going to sit in this wooden groove.

00:16:53.920 --> 00:16:57.560
To make a nice and airtight connection,
between the glass and the wood...

00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:01.240
We're going to put foam
strips in the wooden groove.

00:17:02.880 --> 00:17:07.480
When the glass is in place, 
we're going to secure it with a glazing bar.

00:17:08.640 --> 00:17:13.120
And, the glazing bar has these foam strips as well
to secure the glass.

00:17:14.717 --> 00:17:22.600
It's a little bit off the edge, so you have a nice space 
for silicon to go, and make a watertight connection!

00:17:41.320 --> 00:17:47.080
Around the window frame, we're making a nice granite edge.

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:52.560
To close the bricks, and to finish it off nice!

00:17:54.199 --> 00:17:55.638
- Let’s get it up!

00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:20.939
It's hot!

00:18:20.939 --> 00:18:21.853
- Hot!

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:23.059
Very hot!

00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:26.760
And, a small hole, I see?

00:18:26.760 --> 00:18:29.760
- A really small hole.

00:18:58.680 --> 00:19:01.969
The granite is in place all the way around!

00:19:05.280 --> 00:19:06.378
The final cleaning!

00:19:07.541 --> 00:19:10.541
The window is ready.

00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:13.560
Granite is ready.

00:19:13.560 --> 00:19:16.560
- One, two, three...

00:20:00.280 --> 00:20:02.000
Cool! That was it!

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:03.360
Window is in place.

00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:04.692
View is in place.

00:20:05.425 --> 00:20:06.985
Glass is in place.

00:20:06.985 --> 00:20:08.640
The walls are closed.

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:10.760
And, that was it for this week!

00:20:10.760 --> 00:20:11.800
Thank you for watching!

00:20:11.800 --> 00:20:15.200
If you want to know more about this ruin,
you can go to the research topic.

00:20:15.200 --> 00:20:16.447
You can find the link below.

00:20:17.054 --> 00:20:19.096
And, see you next week!

